416	    /**
417	     * The owner's stored E.164 {@code telephone} formatted for humans, derived on read: the
418	     * leading {@code '+'} and country code, a space, then the national digits grouped in threes
419	     * (e.g. {@code '+61 412 345 678'} for a stored {@code '+61412345678'}). The recognised
420	     * country codes are {@code '+61'} (Australia) and {@code '+1'} (NANP); any other prefix falls
421	     * back to a two-digit country code. The raw {@code telephone} is left in E.164 form.
422	     *
423	     * @return the human-formatted telephone, or the raw value when it is not in E.164 form
424	     */
425	    @Transient
